2026-11-14T00:01:52.2654619Z # LexMachina Factory Architecture
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2655025Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2655527Z ## Current product architecture
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2655760Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2656072Z LexMachina is a **query-specific visual legal-research system**.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2656448Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2656691Z Canonical data flow:
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2656907Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2657117Z ```
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2657480Z legal question
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2657958Z   -> OpenCaseLaw retrieval / citation expansion
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2658466Z   -> normalized query_result_bundle
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2658972Z   -> reranking / source packing
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2659432Z   -> generative sourced answer
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2659975Z   -> independent counter-authority pass
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2660505Z   -> query-conditioned clustering / projection
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2661326Z   -> interactive map + decision/source inspection
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2661855Z ```
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2662026Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2662359Z The product does NOT require one universal geometry for all Swiss case law.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2662889Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2663742Z OpenCaseLaw is the default Swiss public data plane. The legacy 174k LexMachina corpus, global-map artifacts and research results are preserved as reusable evidence/components, not as the MVP critical path.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2664863Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2665095Z ## Central integration contract: query_result_bundle
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2665445Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2666035Z All parallel work should converge on a small product-owned bundle contract rather than inventing incompatible pipelines.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2666636Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2666914Z Minimum conceptual fields:
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2667344Z - query + query variants/provenance;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2667852Z - generated answer + cited decision IDs;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2669052Z - decisions with stable decision_id, canonical URL/citation, court/date/language and retrieved text/snippets;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2669959Z - retrieval/rerank scores and source provenance;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2670719Z - counter-authority status + uncertainty/evidence;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2671560Z - cluster ID/label;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2671960Z - projection coordinates;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2672467Z - citation/typed relations.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2672720Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2673219Z Product may evolve the exact schema while preserving backwards-compatible fixtures during the MVP.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2673844Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2674143Z ## Reuse-first product shell
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2674510Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2675114Z The accepted `lab/product` implementation is a component library, not discarded legacy.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2675749Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2675910Z Prefer adapting:
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2676453Z - threaded HTTP server, caching and error handling;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2677096Z - search/navigation/decision/citation/neighbor API patterns;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2677682Z - WebGL + Canvas rendering;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2678159Z - cluster/decision inspection;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2678603Z - spatial index, LOD and culling;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2679151Z - TF-IDF / clustering / UMAP / Leiden utilities;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2679671Z - multilingual/evaluation helpers.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2680001Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2680549Z Do not rebuild these unless old global-174k assumptions make adaptation slower than isolation behind the query_result_bundle seam.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2681568Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2681839Z ## Parallel engineering topology
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2682113Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2682579Z ### Core Product — continuous integrator
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2683228Z Owns the runnable application and end-to-end contract. It:
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2683808Z - builds its own vertical slice continuously;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2684346Z - inspects ACCEPTED Frontier mounts every cycle;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2684964Z - absorbs useful components immediately;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2685475Z - never waits for every Frontier team;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2685980Z - keeps running until `human_gate_ready=true`.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2686352Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2686935Z ### Core Evaluation — continuous falsifier
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2688467Z Owns compact executable benchmarks for retrieval, counter-authority recall, source validity, language robustness, answer citation validity, cluster stability, reproducibility and latency. It feeds concrete failures back to Product without blocking the first clickable slice.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2689895Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2690213Z ### Human-authorized Frontier engineering teams
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2691207Z Current portfolio may run independent non-overlapping implementation tracks such as:
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2691938Z - OpenCaseLaw retrieval/cache adapter;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2692537Z - generative answer + adversarial/counter-authority engine;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2693129Z - query-map UI adapter.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2693439Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2694085Z Frontier artifacts live in their own namespace and are promoted only after independent audit. Product remains the integrator.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2694753Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2694979Z ## Legacy core lanes
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2695188Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2695394Z ### Corpus
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2696275Z Historical corpus acquisition/normalization work is preserved and PAUSED. Reopen only for a concrete product capability missing from OpenCaseLaw.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2697075Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2697224Z ### Legal Distance
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2698227Z Historical representation/distance research is preserved and PAUSED. Reopen only if query-specific retrieval/map tests expose a precise representation deficit.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2699105Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2699306Z ### Fractal Map
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2700355Z Historical global hierarchy work is preserved and PAUSED. Reuse clustering/rendering code; do not repair the universal 174k map unless a query-specific product need proves it necessary.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2701730Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2701931Z ## Control plane
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2702191Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2703104Z `main` owns mission, agents, workflows, directives and factory direction. Persistent lab branches execute the latest control plane from `main`; stale role definitions on lab branches are not authoritative.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2704267Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2704851Z A cycle works on an isolated branch. Independent audit gates promotion. Rejected work never silently becomes accepted state.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2705644Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2705950Z Accepted branches:
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2706409Z - `lab/corpus`
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2706829Z - `lab/legal-distance`
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2707419Z - `lab/fractal-map`
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2707832Z - `lab/evaluation`
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2708221Z - `lab/product`
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2708632Z - dynamic `lab/frontier/<team_id>`
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2709023Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2709236Z ## Autonomous throughput doctrine
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2709529Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2709997Z Repository-owner attention is the scarce resource; autonomous agent cycles are cheap.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2710510Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2710774Z Therefore:
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2711596Z - direction changes cancel superseded same-lane work;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2712375Z - technical/network/model failures retry or rotate automatically;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2713275Z - multiple healthy free OpenCode models should be load-balanced when available;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2714071Z - independent engineering tracks run in parallel;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2715007Z - Product integrates incrementally rather than waiting for portfolio completion;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2715857Z - agents choose libraries/layouts/thresholds/repair strategies autonomously;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2716902Z - human escalation is reserved for a ready-to-test product or an unavoidable owner-level product/business/legal/external-access decision.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2717619Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2717830Z ## Output layout
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2718524Z - lane implementation: `corpus/`, `legal_distance/`, `fractal_map/`, `evaluation/`, `product/`
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2719275Z - tests: `tests/<lane>/`
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2719933Z - immutable outputs: `results/<lane>/`
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2720386Z - reports: `reports/<lane>/`
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2721097Z - accepted lane state: `state/<lane>.json`
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2721679Z - lane directives: `directives/lanes/<lane>.md`
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2722438Z - dynamic Frontier: `frontier/<team>/`, `results/frontier/<team>/`, `state/frontier/<team>.json`
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2722921Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2723103Z ## Invariants
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2723749Z - At most one active run per core lane or Frontier team, but different lanes/teams should run in parallel.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2724621Z - Newer direction/charter work supersedes stale same-lane/team work.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2725274Z - PASS required for accepted promotion.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2725962Z - Audit REVISE means concrete repair; BLOCKED prevents dishonest loops.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2726628Z - Supervisor dispatch is idempotent.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2727195Z - A repair cannot succeed with zero durable delta.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2727831Z - Historical accepted/negative evidence is preserved.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2728823Z - Human-authorized Frontier charters remain active until their stop/promote rule is met or an ACCEPTED equivalent supersedes them.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2730007Z - Product does not stop at a partial milestone; `human_gate_ready=true` is the normal handoff point.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2730653Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2731091Z ## Active vs historical control state
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2733244Z `state/frontier_portfolio.json` contains only executable/current Frontier teams. Retired/superseded charters are moved intact to `state/archive/frontier_portfolio_history.json`; their full implementation/audit evidence remains on lab/cycle branches. Active blockers live only under `state/blockers/`; retired blockers belong under `state/archive/blockers/`.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2737663Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2739470Z `main` is deliberately lightweight. Full result arrays, parquet files, benchmark dumps and historical reports must NOT be mirrored to main. `results/accepted-state/` plus `results/ACCEPTED_CATALOG.json` are the compact accepted-state index; detailed artifacts live on the accepted lab branch that produced them.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2741199Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2741382Z ## Progressive query execution
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2751324Z The UI should become useful in stages instead of blocking on one monolithic request:
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2752534Z 1. retrieve/dedupe broad candidates;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2753081Z 2. render an initial query map;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2753733Z 3. enrich selected evidence and stream/generate the sourced answer;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2754406Z 4. run adversarial retrieval/classification;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2755037Z 5. patch counter-authorities/relations into the existing bundle/map.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2755567Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2756682Z The broad map pool and LLM evidence pack are deliberately different sizes. Query-specific mode must not load global 174k matrices on startup. Full-text decision bodies are lazy. Expensive geometry is cached by retrieval/config hash.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2758194Z =====PROTOCOL=====
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2758745Z # Research Protocol
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2758976Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2759300Z Every research cycle answers one bounded question that can change a product or research decision.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2759668Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2759900Z 1. Read the Master Prompt, current factory direction and lane directive.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2760454Z 2. Inspect relevant ACCEPTED evidence from other lanes/frontiers.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2761140Z 3. State hypothesis, baseline and product decision unlocked.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2761706Z 4. Freeze claim-bearing sample, metric and success rule before observing result.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2762264Z 5. Implement the smallest rigorous discriminating experiment.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2762714Z 6. Run it; preserve raw outputs and failures.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2763207Z 7. Compare with baseline and report uncertainty/failure modes.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2763687Z 8. Write machine-readable lane state plus human-readable report.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2764404Z 9. Recommend CONTINUE, PIVOT_WITHIN_MISSION, BLOCKED, PRODUCTIZE or PAUSE.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2764718Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2765400Z Preferred baselines include whole-document generic embedding, legal embedding/Isaacus-style baseline where accessible, lexical retrieval, citation-only, norms-only and simple hybrids before complex learned methods.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2766156Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2767008Z Core evaluation families: Jurivoc/human-index agreement where available; nearest-neighbor legal relevance; known-lineage recovery; no-explicit-citation lineage recovery; boilerplate resistance; multilingual invariance; corpus-scale stability; hierarchy coherence; and human preference.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2767991Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2768177Z ## Mandatory accepted-state fields
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2770676Z Every core research lane must keep `state/<lane>.json` machine-readable and set at least: `lane`, `direction_version`, `evidence_tier`, `cycle_status`, `continue_recommended`, `accepted_run_id` (or proposed run id before audit), `evidence_refs`, and `next_recommendation`. `continue_recommended=true` means another cycle under the SAME factory-direction question has a concrete discriminating purpose; it is not a generic request to keep running. When no additional same-question cycle is justified, set it false so the Factory Director can decide the successor question.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2772577Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2773195Z Frontier states must analogously preserve `team_id`, `charter_version`, `evidence_tier`, `cycle_status`, `continue_recommended`, provenance/evidence references and the charter stop/promote recommendation.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2773902Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2774072Z ## Product-engineering cycles
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2775261Z Product and engineering Frontier cycles are not required to manufacture a scientific hypothesis when the task is implementation. They must instead state the concrete capability/integration contract, reuse available accepted components, produce runnable code/tests/fixtures, and verify the acceptance contract.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2776239Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2776738Z For the query-map MVP, do not require obsolete universal-174k metrics to gate query-specific components. Evaluate the capability actually being shipped.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2777322Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2777454Z ## Owner-attention / continuation
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2779724Z Autonomous cycles may continue while they produce measurable executable progress. Do not use `continue_recommended=false` on Product merely because one intermediate milestone completed. Product should remain `continue_recommended=true` until it records `human_gate_ready=true` for a locally runnable end-to-end product, unless the current direction is genuinely superseded or structurally blocked.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2781797Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2782521Z Technical failures, provider failures, library choices and ordinary implementation decisions are not human blockers. Retry, rotate, narrow or reroute autonomously.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.2783693Z [0m
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3614475Z [0m$ [0mcat /tmp/lex_control/AGENTS.md; echo "=====MASTER====="; cat /tmp/lex_control/LEXMACHINA_MASTER_PROMPT.md
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3615471Z # LexMachina Agent Constitution
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3615939Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3616666Z This file and `LEXMACHINA_MASTER_PROMPT.md` are binding for every OpenCode/Ox agent.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3617323Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3618089Z 1. The product mission is immutable unless a human changes the Main Prompt on `main`.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3619449Z 2. Every configured custom agent MUST have exactly one active canonical card in `docs/agents/AGENT_CARDS.md`.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3621138Z 3. An agent may perform broad methods inside its role, but may not redefine its role, lane, evidence standard, product goal or write scope.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3622907Z 4. Fresh-context subagents are encouraged when they increase throughput or adversarial coverage. They do not inherit authority to change the parent mission.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3624751Z 5. Accepted evidence beats narrative. Negative results remain evidence.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3626326Z 6. No agent may weaken a frozen benchmark, delete contrary outputs, overwrite historical claim-bearing results, or treat a prettier map as better without evaluation.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3628320Z 7. No agent may spend cycles on unrelated legal-AI ideas. Every substantive task must connect directly to the canonical query-specific answer + counter-authority + visual-map product or its evaluation.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3630186Z 8. If a card conflicts with the Main Prompt, the Main Prompt wins. If a workflow scope is narrower than a card, the workflow wins.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3631681Z 9. Agents never ask for interactive approval inside autonomous workflows. Record blockers instead.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3633678Z 10. `main` is the control plane. Persistent lab branches may contain stale copies; the workflow-mounted control plane from `main` is authoritative.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3635144Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3636252Z 11. REUSE-FIRST: before rebuilding a capability, agents must inspect existing LexMachina code/results and open infrastructure. Preserve and adapt useful work; the pivot changes the critical path, not history.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3638432Z 12. TIME-TO-CLICKABLE: product work prioritizes executable vertical slices over architecture prose. A normal product cycle with no runnable delta is invalid unless externally blocked.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3639616Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3641144Z 13. OWNER-ATTENTION: autonomous compute/cycles are cheap; the repository owner's attention is scarce. Resolve technical choices, failures and retries autonomously. Human escalation is reserved for a ready-to-test product or a genuinely unavoidable owner-level decision.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3643242Z =====MASTER=====
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3644137Z # LEXMACHINA — MASTER PROMPT
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3644581Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3644845Z ## Mission
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3645716Z Build the fastest path to a genuinely useful **visual legal research interface** for Swiss case law.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3646485Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3647218Z LexMachina is not required to discover one universal geometry of all jurisprudence. Its core product is query-specific:
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3648054Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3649175Z > legal question → broad retrieval → sourced AI answer → visual map of the relevant jurisprudence → explicit search for contrary / limiting authority.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3650574Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3651637Z The map exists to help jurists see branches, minority lines, exceptions, isolated decisions and relationships that a ranked text list or a single AI answer can hide.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3652721Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3653052Z ## Initial product scope
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3653762Z 1. Swiss case law as the first public domain.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3654908Z 2. Use **OpenCaseLaw public infrastructure as the default data source** instead of rebuilding the national corpus and citation graph.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3656318Z 3. For each query, retrieve broadly, preserve high recall, then build a map over a tractable result set.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3657643Z 4. Keep the AI answer and the visual map side by side: the map is an audit/exploration layer for the answer.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3658984Z 5. Explicitly search for decisions that contradict, limit, distinguish or create exceptions to the provisional answer.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3660346Z 6. Ship a clickable end-to-end prototype before doing more fundamental representation research.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3661766Z 7. User-imported corpora remain a later capability, not the MVP critical path.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3662439Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3662625Z ## Central product question
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3664493Z For a real legal research query, does **AI answer + visual query map** help a jurist discover and understand relevant jurisprudence — especially contrary or minority authority — better than an AI answer plus a conventional ranked list?
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3665952Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3666534Z Everything in this repository exists to answer that question and turn a positive answer into product capability.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3666974Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3667133Z ## Query-conditioned structure
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3667656Z Do not assume every decision has one globally correct position in a universal legal space.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3668026Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3668385Z The relevant structure is allowed to depend on the current research question, active relation layer and retrieved candidate set.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3668841Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3669162Z The same decision may occupy a different position for a different query. This is expected.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3669499Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3669674Z ## Retrieval-first doctrine
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3670090Z A visualization cannot reveal an authority that retrieval failed to find.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3670405Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3670559Z Therefore:
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3671087Z - optimize recall before map aesthetics;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3671614Z - search across FR/DE/IT;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3672042Z - use norms, citations and query expansion where useful;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3672671Z - preserve lower-ranked candidates that may represent contrary or minority lines;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3673422Z - run an independent adversarial retrieval pass against the provisional answer.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3673827Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3674029Z ## Adversarial research requirement
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3674684Z For every substantive research query, the product should attempt to find authority that could:
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3675379Z - contradict the provisional answer;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3675800Z - narrow it;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3676215Z - distinguish the facts or legal issue;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3676923Z - reveal an exception;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3677324Z - expose an older/minority line;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3677912Z - reveal a language-specific branch.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3678220Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3678772Z These authorities must remain visible in the result set even when they are not top-ranked by the initial search.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3679408Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3679944Z Never classify a case as supporting/contrary/limiting unless the evidence supports that label.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3680572Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3680741Z ## Visual map requirement
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3681560Z The map is a research interface, not decoration.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3681990Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3682186Z Minimum semantics:
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3682624Z - point = decision;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3683193Z - proximity = query-conditioned similarity/relation;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3683842Z - cluster = coherent group of retrieved decisions;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3684500Z - outlier = weakly connected/isolated result worth inspecting;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3685269Z - relations/citations can be revealed on selection;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3685944Z - cluster labels explain why a group exists;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3686588Z - counter-authorities are visually discoverable.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3686964Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3687587Z 2D or 3D is an implementation choice. A 3D point cloud is not inherently better. Use 3D only if it improves comprehension.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3688607Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3688805Z ## Data-source doctrine
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3690129Z Prefer open, maintained infrastructure over rebuilding commoditized components.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3690702Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3692006Z For Swiss public law research, OpenCaseLaw is the canonical first source for the MVP because it provides public search, decision records, laws and citation infrastructure.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3692924Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3694162Z Preserve the legacy LexMachina 174k corpus and all accepted/rejected research results as historical evidence and optional fallback/test data, but do not keep them on the critical path unless the new product actually needs them.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3695343Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3695551Z ## Owner-time invariant
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3696219Z The scarce development resource is **the repository owner's attention**, not autonomous agent compute.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3697315Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3698352Z For development/testing, use free OpenCode models, local open-source models, OpenCaseLaw public infrastructure and existing repository assets so the owner is not required to provision paid APIs just to evaluate the MVP.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3699624Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3700353Z This does NOT constrain the eventual production stack: a deployed product may use paid/local/hosted LLM, embedding or reranking services when justified.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3701484Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3701873Z The factory must optimize for low owner involvement:
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3702564Z - retry/reroute technical failures autonomously;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3703204Z - choose implementation details autonomously;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3703896Z - reuse existing work before rebuilding;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3704528Z - never ask the owner to supervise ordinary engineering;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3705542Z - surface a human gate only for a ready-to-test product or a genuine product/business/legal/external-access decision.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3706271Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3706452Z ## Broad means, narrow end
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3708230Z The factory may use lexical search, BM25/TF-IDF, multilingual query expansion, citation expansion, open-source embeddings, graph methods, reranking, clustering, projection, WebGL/Canvas, answer generation, counter-authority retrieval and other methods that directly improve the query-map product.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3709961Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3710482Z Do not launch broad research programs merely because they are scientifically interesting.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3711381Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3711552Z Do not rebuild:
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3712244Z - a national Swiss case-law corpus;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3712792Z - a national citation graph;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3713295Z - a universal 174k embedding space;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3713856Z - a universal fractal hierarchy;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3714207Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3714537Z unless a concrete MVP capability cannot be built without it.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3714925Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3715140Z ## Reuse doctrine
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3715711Z Reuse existing LexMachina work when it shortens time-to-product:
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3716332Z - TF-IDF / lexical tooling;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3716875Z - multilingual robustness tests;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3717364Z - clustering and hierarchy code;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3717841Z - WebGL / Canvas rendering;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3718334Z - LOD / culling;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3718840Z - navigation / decision detail components;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3719447Z - evaluation discipline;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3719911Z - negative/null results.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3720166Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3721138Z Legacy join-alignment, dense-embedding and corpus-scale graph problems are not MVP blockers unless they directly affect the query-specific pipeline.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3722149Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3722328Z ## Evaluation doctrine
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3723500Z Before claim-bearing measurement, freeze hypothesis, query set, baseline, metric and success rule. Preserve negative results. Never weaken a benchmark after seeing results.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3724582Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3724807Z Automated evaluation should cover:
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3725417Z - recall of known relevant authorities;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3725997Z - recall of known contrary/limiting authorities;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3726610Z - source validity;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3727023Z - duplication;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3727485Z - language robustness;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3727945Z - reproducibility;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3728362Z - latency;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3728791Z - cluster stability.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3729072Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3729396Z Automated metrics do not prove that the visualization is useful.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3729932Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3730161Z ## Human product gate
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3731355Z Further investment is justified only if real legal research tasks show that the visual layer materially improves the experience over answer + ranked list.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3732811Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3733024Z The key questions are:
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3733867Z 1. Did the map expose a relevant branch, exception or decision that was less visible in the list/answer?
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3734936Z 2. Did the map make the jurisprudential structure easier to understand?
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3735790Z 3. Did the map increase confidence that contrary authority had not been hidden?
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3736762Z 4. Was the combined answer + map preferable to the conventional interface?
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3737304Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3737554Z If not, stop the standalone product.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3737857Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3738116Z ## Product doctrine
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3738685Z Build the smallest clickable end-to-end slice first.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3739065Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3739285Z Canonical implementation order:
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3739849Z 1. free OpenCaseLaw retrieval + caching;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3740414Z 2. free reranking / result bundle;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3741064Z 3. sourced AI answer;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3741612Z 4. independent counter-authority pass;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3742533Z 5. query-specific interactive map over roughly 100–300 decisions;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3743257Z 6. frozen automated tests;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3743730Z 7. human product test.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3743984Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3744740Z Only after this gate should the factory invest in more sophisticated global geometry, dense embeddings, custom corpus infrastructure or 3D.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3745644Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3746026Z The authoritative MVP specification is `docs/product/QUERY_MAP_MVP.md`.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3746564Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3746729Z ## Evidence tiers
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3747994Z UNTESTED < EXPLORATORY < REPRODUCED < ACCEPTED. Only ACCEPTED findings may raise default product claims. Accepted negative findings are first-class results.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3748994Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3749214Z ## Non-negotiables
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3749929Z - Preserve provenance and historical results; never overwrite claim-bearing outputs.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3751030Z - Never fabricate data, labels, citations or results.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3751706Z - Never weaken a benchmark after seeing results.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3752448Z - Never equate prettier visualization with better legal navigation.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3753515Z - Do not require the owner to provision paid APIs merely to develop/test the MVP; future production inference may be paid or local.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3754720Z - Technical failures auto-retry/recover; dead ends reroute. Only a genuine human decision may stop the factory.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.3755745Z - Stay on the product mission.
