2026-11-14T00:01:52.4180789Z =====PRODUCT LANE=====
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4181452Z # Product lane — query-map fast path
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4181736Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4182263Z Ship the shortest runnable path to the canonical query-map MVP in `docs/product/QUERY_MAP_MVP.md`, while minimizing repository-owner attention.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4182824Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4183010Z ## REUSE-FIRST mandate
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4184017Z Before writing replacement infrastructure, inspect the existing `lab/product` implementation and accepted peer mounts. Reuse working components whenever they shorten time-to-clickable-product. In particular, prefer adapting the existing:
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4185169Z - stdlib threaded HTTP server and response cache;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4185760Z - search / decision-detail / citation / neighbor API patterns;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4186254Z - WebGL + Canvas frontend;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4186640Z - clustering / Leiden / UMAP utilities;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4187192Z - map loading, navigation, LOD / culling and spatial-index patterns;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4187782Z - multilingual robustness and proximity/evaluation utilities.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4188122Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4188627Z Do NOT rebuild these just because the product mission changed. Delete/replace code only when the old global-174k assumptions make reuse slower than adaptation.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4189294Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4189422Z ## Product fast path
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4189823Z The first priority is a runnable vertical slice, not a report.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4190131Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4190429Z A valid producer cycle must materially advance executable code toward:
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4191524Z question -> OpenCaseLaw retrieval/cache -> query result bundle -> free reranking -> sourced generative answer -> independent counter-authority pass -> query-specific clickable map.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4192187Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4192459Z For the first clickable slice, simple and correct beats sophisticated:
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4193241Z - target roughly 100–300 retrieved decisions;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4193675Z - TF-IDF/BM25 + citation expansion is acceptable;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4194167Z - simple deterministic clustering/projection is acceptable;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4194722Z - reuse the current frontend rather than redesigning it;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4195280Z - 2D is acceptable; 3D is explicitly NOT a blocker;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4195946Z - a cached OpenCaseLaw fixture is acceptable for deterministic tests while live retrieval remains available.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4196396Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4196580Z ## Anti-overengineering
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4196927Z Do NOT spend an MVP cycle on:
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4197300Z - universal 174k alignment;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4197707Z - rebuilding the Swiss corpus/citation graph;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4198134Z - dense 174k embedding generation;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4198511Z - global fractal hierarchy;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4198887Z - custom model training;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4199339Z - requiring the owner to provision paid inference for development/testing;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4199838Z - cosmetic redesign;
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4200240Z - broad architecture prose before a vertical slice exists.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4200545Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4200678Z ## Cycle output requirement
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4201584Z Every normal product cycle must leave runnable code or tests. A cycle that produces only plans/reports/specs is REVISE unless execution is genuinely externally blocked.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4202250Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4203663Z The first successful product cycle should, at minimum, allow a developer to run one local command/server, submit or select a real Swiss-law query fixture, and see a source-linked clickable result map. Generative answer/counter-authority functionality should be added in the same cycle if feasible; otherwise it is the immediate next delta.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4204777Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4205609Z Do not involve the owner during ordinary implementation/debugging. Continue autonomously through retries, narrower slices and repairs until there is a genuinely clickable end-to-end artifact worth testing, or an unavoidable owner-level decision.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4206500Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4206642Z ## Owner-attention rule
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4207842Z Agent cycles are cheap; owner attention is expensive. There is no fixed cycle limit while executable progress continues. If a cycle stalls, diagnose and reroute autonomously. Do not ask the owner to choose technical details or babysit failures. The next normal owner interaction should be a usable product test.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4208944Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4209121Z ## Parallel integration rule
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4210345Z Three human-authorized Frontier engineering teams may produce retrieval, generative-audit, and query-map UI components in parallel. Do NOT wait for all teams. At the start of every product cycle, inspect ACCEPTED mounts under /tmp/lex_accepted/frontier and immediately absorb any component that passes its integration contract.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4211548Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4212101Z Product remains responsible for the end-to-end app and may implement the same missing seam itself if a Frontier team is slow. Frontier teams are accelerators, not dependencies.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4212746Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4213524Z Until the product state explicitly records `human_gate_ready: true` with a locally runnable question -> sourced answer -> counter-authority -> clickable map path, keep `continue_recommended: true`. A partial milestone is not a reason for the lane to stop.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4214379Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4214552Z ## Runtime performance mandate
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4215948Z The query-map hot path must be lightweight. Do not initialize legacy 174k representations on default server startup. Render the first query-specific candidate map before waiting for the LLM/counter-authority pass. Fetch full decisions lazily for the evidence subset/clicked cases, not all mapped cases. Use persistent cache + bounded concurrency + deterministic cache/config hashes.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4217234Z 
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4219103Z Target: cached map <1s; after the first upstream search page arrives, local map overhead <1.5s; render the first ~50–100 results immediately and expand toward 100–300 in background; local 100–300 point geometry <2s; detail click <150ms where data is local. Measure upstream OpenCaseLaw latency separately rather than blaming local code. Treat these as engineering budgets and measure them. Prefer simpler clustering/projection when sophistication misses the budget without demonstrated UX benefit.
2026-11-14T00:01:52.4220785Z =====ACCEPTED=====
