2026-11-14T00:03:14.4758242Z #!/usr/bin/env python3
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4758737Z """Frozen D2/D3/D4 content-defect re-probe over the committed bundle family.
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4759190Z 
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4759313Z Why this exists
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4759700Z ---------------
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4760011Z Direction v68 ordered work item (2) asks the product to *publish* a per-bundle
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4760479Z and per-class histogram of the frozen D2/D3/D4 content predicates over the
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4761202Z flagship offline/server slice family, together with the false-reject count on
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4761641Z the confirmed set, instead of restating the result as prose in
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4762056Z ``state/product.json``.  Until this module existed the only statement of that
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4762415Z result was the narrative line
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4762565Z 
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4762751Z     "All 4 offline slice bundles and the server slice bundle regenerated with
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4763107Z      the fix show correct downgrades"
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4763277Z 
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4763624Z which no committed instrument re-derived.  This module is that instrument.
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4763899Z 
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4764027Z What it measures (and what it deliberately does not)
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4764351Z ----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4764729Z For every committed ``*.bundle.json`` under ``results/product/offline_slice/``
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4765173Z and ``results/product/server_slice/`` it applies the product's own frozen
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4765655Z content predicates (``product.query.counter_evidence_span.frozen_content_defects``)
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4766143Z to every row that is still ``counter_evidence_verified is True`` and counts the
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4766575Z defect classes that survive on the *shipped* (post-filter) bytes.
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4766819Z 
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4767047Z * ``fixed_path_family`` — bundles whose provenance carries
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4767465Z   ``provenance.counter_evidence_span.content_filter``, i.e. bundles that were
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4767949Z   regenerated on the fixed path.  This family is *identified from the bytes*,
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4768395Z   never hard-coded, so a future regeneration is picked up automatically.
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4768901Z * ``all_committed`` — every committed bundle, including historical ones that
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4769360Z   predate the fix.  Historical defects are preserved evidence, not a defect of
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4769814Z   the current head; both populations are published side by side so the two are
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4770161Z   never conflated.
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4770521Z * ``before_after`` — for the four decisions the accepted FAST-MVP falsifier
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4771441Z   measured as verified-but-defective, the seam's own per-row downgrade records
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4771949Z   on the fixed path are paired with the historical verified verdict: same
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4772405Z   decision, BEFORE verified+defective, AFTER unevidenced with a reason code.
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4772867Z   The confirmed sound row is re-checked in the same pass.  No historical
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4773228Z   bundle is rewritten or deleted.
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4773646Z * ``packet_v3_reemission`` — the frozen packet-of-record v3 bytes are hashed,
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4774201Z   deep-copied, and re-run through the current baseline and guarded arms.  The
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4774640Z   accepted arm artifact is pinned by sha256 and compared side by side on
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4775084Z   emitted / verified / abstained / support-among-emitted / yield.  Because v3
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4775543Z   carries no *verified defective incumbent*, the v68 rejection leg is expected
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4776000Z   to downgrade zero rows there; that no-op and the one content-clean verbatim
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4776432Z   guarded emission are published explicitly rather than hidden.
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4776666Z 
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4776849Z It imports the frozen predicate constants verbatim through the accepted
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4777306Z ``counter_evidence_span`` module and re-publishes their provenance hashes.  It
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4777766Z NEVER re-derives, re-tunes or edits the frozen gate, rubric, threshold or bar,
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4778219Z it never runs the evaluation scorer and it makes no serve/admission claim.
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4778488Z 
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4778568Z Claim ceiling
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4778758Z -------------
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4779058Z Reported-only measurement of committed bytes under the frozen content
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4779496Z predicates.  It says nothing about legal usefulness, nothing about a frozen
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4779953Z scorer's emission predicate (factory-wide requirement 26 keeps those families
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4780415Z separate), and nothing about bundles outside this repository.
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4780658Z 
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4780736Z Usage
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4781022Z -----
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4781291Z     python3 product/content_family_probe.py --run-id 40143042888
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4781649Z     python3 product/content_family_probe.py --json
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4782110Z     python3 product/content_family_probe.py --check     # exit 1 when unmet
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4782452Z """
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4782652Z from __future__ import annotations
2026-11-14T00:03:14.4782814Z 
